OL,3,GNEWSA'This doesn't happen to us' - mum
OL,4,Aon child's cancer
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe mother of a five-year-old girl has
OL,7,Fspoken of the shock she felt when her
OL,8,Fdaughter was diagnosed with leukaemia.
OL,10,F"I thought, this doesn't happen to us,
OL,11,Fthis is what happens to other people,"
OL,12,Fsaid Sam about the moment she found out
OL,13,Fdaughter Nina, from Peterborough, was
OL,14,Fsuffering from cancer days, just days
OL,15,Fafter she had started school.
OL,17,FSam had become concerned about Nina's
OL,18,Fpersistent bruising and lack of energy,
OL,19,Fand now hoped to raise awareness about
OL,20,Fthe disease during September's
OL,21,FChildhood Cancer Awareness Month.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,374,370,200,160,0,100
